CM_ BU_ Tritium "Tritium WaveSculptor motor controller: drives the motor and reports its speed, currents, voltages and temperatures. Its messages in this file use base address 0x600 (0x600 to 0x617), as seen in Tests/data/NRT.BIN. TODO: add the controller model and firmware version fitted to Peri.";
CM_ BU_ Tritium_Right "Second (right) motor controller, from an earlier two-motor set-up. TODO: add whether Peri has a second motor controller; if not, remove its messages (0x80 to 0x8E) from this file.";
CM_ BU_ DriverControls "Driver controls: send the driver's drive and power commands to the motor controller (base address 0x500).";
CM_ BU_ DriverControls_Right "Driver controls for the second (right) motor controller, from an earlier two-motor set-up. TODO: add whether Peri uses these; if not, remove their messages (0x41 to 0x43) from this file.";
CM_ BO_ 3221225472 "Placeholder created by the Vector DBC editor to hold signals that are not in any message. Never sent on the bus.";
CM_ SG_ 3221225472 Reserved2 "Not used.";
CM_ BO_ 1536 "Motor controller identification. Sent once a second.";
CM_ SG_ 1536 TritiumId "Device identifier, fixed for the model (sent as the characters TRIa on some models).";
CM_ SG_ 1536 SerialNumber "Device serial number, allocated at manufacture.";
CM_ BO_ 1537 "Motor controller status: which limits are active, errors, and CAN error counts.";
CM_ SG_ 1537 ActiveMotor "Index of the motor profile currently in use.";
CM_ SG_ 1537 ErrorFlags "Error flags, one bit each (bit 0 hardware over current, bit 1 software over current, bit 2 DC bus over voltage, bit 3 bad motor position hall sequence, bit 4 watchdog caused the last reset, bit 5 config read error, bit 6 15 V rail under voltage lock out). 0 = no errors. TODO: add the remaining bits from the WaveSculptor22 user manual.";
CM_ SG_ 1537 LimitFlags "Which limit is currently restricting the controller's output, one bit each (bit 0 bridge PWM, bit 1 motor current, bit 2 velocity, bit 3 bus current, bit 4 bus voltage upper limit, bit 5 bus voltage lower limit, bit 6 heatsink temperature).";
CM_ SG_ 1537 TransmitErrorCount "Number of CAN transmit errors counted by the controller.";
CM_ SG_ 1537 ReceiveErrorCount "Number of CAN receive errors counted by the controller.";
CM_ BO_ 257 "Left motor controller status. From an earlier two-motor set-up (separate left and right controllers). Not seen in Tests/data/NRT.BIN. TODO: add whether Peri uses this message; if not, remove it from this file.";
CM_ SG_ 257 ActiveMotor "Index of the motor profile currently in use.";
CM_ SG_ 257 ErrorFlagHWOvercurrent "1 = hardware over current error.";
CM_ SG_ 257 ErrorFlagSWOvercurrent "1 = software over current error.";
CM_ SG_ 257 ErrorFlagDCBusOvervoltage "1 = DC bus over voltage error.";
CM_ SG_ 257 ErrorFlagMotorPositionHallSequence "1 = bad motor position hall sequence error.";
CM_ SG_ 257 ErrorFlagWatchdog "1 = the watchdog caused the last reset.";
CM_ SG_ 257 ErrorFlagConfigRead "1 = config read error (some settings may have been reset to defaults).";
CM_ SG_ 257 ErrorFlag15VUndervoltage "1 = a 15 V rail under voltage lock out occurred.";
CM_ SG_ 257 LimitFlagBridgePWM "1 = output is being limited by the bridge PWM.";
CM_ SG_ 257 LimitFlagMotorCurrent "1 = output is being limited by the motor current limit.";
CM_ SG_ 257 LimitFlagVelocity "1 = output is being limited by the velocity limit.";
CM_ SG_ 257 LimitFlagBusCurrent "1 = output is being limited by the bus current limit.";
CM_ SG_ 257 LimitFlagBusVoltageUpperLimit "1 = output is being limited by the bus voltage upper limit.";
CM_ SG_ 257 LimitFlagBusVoltageLowerLimit "1 = output is being limited by the bus voltage lower limit.";
CM_ SG_ 257 LimitFlagHeatsinkTemperature "1 = output is being limited by the heatsink temperature.";
CM_ BO_ 1538 "Battery-side (DC bus) voltage and current at the motor controller.";
CM_ SG_ 1538 BusVoltage "DC bus (battery) voltage at the controller.";
CM_ SG_ 1538 BusCurrent "Current drawn from the DC bus (battery) by the controller.";
CM_ BO_ 1539 "Motor speed and vehicle speed.";
CM_ SG_ 1539 MotorVelocity "Motor speed in revolutions per minute.";
CM_ SG_ 1539 VehicleVelocity "Vehicle speed in metres per second, calculated by the controller from the motor speed and the wheel size set in its configuration.";
CM_ BO_ 1540 "Current in two of the motor's three phases.";
CM_ SG_ 1540 PhaseBCurrent "RMS current in motor phase B.";
CM_ SG_ 1540 PhaseCCurrent "RMS current in motor phase C.";
CM_ BO_ 1541 "Voltage applied to the motor, as a vector (mainly for motor tuning).";
CM_ SG_ 1541 VectVoltImag "Imaginary component of the voltage vector applied to the motor.";
CM_ SG_ 1541 VectVoltReal "Real component of the voltage vector applied to the motor.";
CM_ BO_ 1542 "Current in the motor, as a vector (mainly for motor tuning).";
CM_ SG_ 1542 VectCurrImag "Imaginary component of the motor current vector. This is the current that produces torque.";
CM_ SG_ 1542 VectCurrReal "Real component of the motor current vector: the field current of the motor.";
CM_ BO_ 1543 "Back-EMF (the voltage generated by the spinning motor), as a vector.";
CM_ SG_ 1543 PeakBackEmfPhaseToNeutral "Peak phase to neutral back-EMF voltage of the motor.";
CM_ SG_ 1543 BackEmfD "By definition always 0 V.";
CM_ BO_ 1544 "Voltage of the controller's internal 15 V supply rail.";
CM_ SG_ 1544 Reserved "Reserved, not used.";
CM_ SG_ 1544 FifteenVSupply "Actual voltage of the internal 15 V supply rail.";
CM_ BO_ 1545 "Voltages of the controller's internal 3.3 V and 1.9 V supply rails.";
CM_ SG_ 1545 ThreeThreeVSupply "Actual voltage of the internal 3.3 V supply rail.";
CM_ SG_ 1545 OneNineVSupply "Actual voltage of the internal 1.9 V (processor) supply rail.";
CM_ BO_ 1546 "Cooling fan drive and speed (WaveSculptor20 layout). Marked reserved and not active in Tests/data/CANBusConfig.xlsm, and not seen in Tests/data/NRT.BIN. TODO: add whether Peri's motor controller sends this message; if not, remove it.";
CM_ SG_ 1546 VoltagePercentage "Drive voltage to the cooling fan, in percent. Above 0 % the fan should be spinning.";
CM_ SG_ 1546 FanSpeed "Cooling fan speed in revolutions per minute.";
CM_ BO_ 1547 "Motor and controller heatsink temperatures.";
CM_ SG_ 1547 MotorTemp "Internal temperature of the motor.";
CM_ SG_ 1547 HeatSinkTemp "Surface temperature of the controller's heatsink.";
CM_ BO_ 1548 "Temperature of the controller's processor board.";
CM_ SG_ 1548 DspBoardTemp "Temperature of the controller's processor (DSP) board.";
CM_ SG_ 1548 Reserved "Reserved, not used.";
